sia during 2005–2006 (351 cases), Bangladesh in 2006 (18 cases), and Burma during 2006–2007 (11 cases).","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":822,"renderedHeight":550,"naturalWidth":822,"naturalHeight":550,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 506 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":14588},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m6342a2f2.gif","alt":"The figure above is a bar chart showing the number of polio cases from wild poliovirus types 1 (WPV1) and 3 (WPV3), by month, in India during January 2001–January 2011. India introduced monovalent OPV type 1 (mOPV1) and type 3 (mOPV3) in 2005. Predominant use of mOPV1 greatly reduced the incidence of WPV1 but allowed increased WPV3 incidence until bivalent OPV types 1 and 3 (bOPV) was introduced in 2010. The intensification of the migrant and transit strategies coupled with predominant use of bOPV was associated with a reduction in both WPV1 and WPV3.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":835,"renderedHeight":520,"naturalWidth":835,"naturalHeight":520,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 557 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":16440},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_pdf.gif","alt":"Adobe PDF file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"naturalWidth":16,"naturalHeight":16,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":6058},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/TemplatePackage/images/icon_word.gif","alt":"Microsoft Word file","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":16,"renderedHeight":16,"nat